<title>UK: Matra Marconi wins Brazil order.</title>
<headline>Matra Marconi wins Brazil order.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Matra Marconi Space, the Anglo-French satellite maker and supplier, said on Friday it had won a contract worth over $10 million to provide an atmposphere humidity sounder for the National Space Research Institute of Brazil.</p>
<p>In a statement the company, co-owned by Lagardere Group's Matra and Britain's General Electric Company Plc, said a signficicant part of the manufacture of the instrument would take place in Brazil.</p>
<p>The sounder, which will produce atmospheric moisture calibration data at a range of altitudes, will be carried on NASA's Earth Observation Satellite-PM1 mission.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
